{"module":"enforcement","voice":"male","duration":179.8,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Immigration enforcement now","start":0.0,"end":1.82,"words":[[0.04,0.78],[0.78,1.45],[1.45,1.68]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Immigration enforcement increasingly runs through local police and 911-style reports.","start":2.62,"end":9.18,"words":[[2.66,3.4],[3.4,4.06],[4.06,4.8],[4.8,5.09],[5.09,5.31],[5.31,5.76],[5.76,6.13],[6.13,6.35],[6.35,8.11],[8.11,8.63]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This lesson covers how that works and what the evidence shows.","start":9.53,"end":13.68,"words":[[9.58,9.83],[9.83,10.23],[10.23,10.64],[10.64,10.88],[10.88,11.13],[11.13,11.45],[11.45,11.7],[11.7,11.94],[11.94,12.1],[12.1,12.67],[12.67,13.08]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The history is in “Borders.”","start":14.03,"end":15.92,"words":[[14.08,14.22],[14.22,14.71],[14.71,14.85],[14.85,15.0],[15.0,15.42]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Local police as immigration agents","start":16.27,"end":19.29,"words":[[16.32,16.86],[16.86,17.3],[17.3,17.48],[17.48,18.38],[18.38,19.09]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Section 287(g) of federal immigration law lets ICE deputize local police and sheriffs to carry out some immigration enforcement.","start":19.99,"end":29.93,"words":[[20.04,20.5],[20.5,22.26],[22.53,22.68],[22.68,23.22],[23.22,23.98],[23.98,24.14],[24.14,24.44],[24.44,24.67],[24.67,25.36],[25.36,25.82],[25.82,26.2],[26.2,26.43],[26.43,26.89],[26.89,27.05],[27.05,27.35],[27.35,27.58],[27.58,27.81],[27.81,28.58],[28.58,29.34]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The number of 287(g) agreements expanded sharply in 2025.","start":30.28,"end":35.47,"words":[[30.33,30.45],[30.45,30.75],[30.75,30.87],[30.87,32.26],[32.47,33.02],[33.02,33.56],[33.56,33.86],[33.86,33.98],[33.98,35.01]]},{"el":"s0","text":"From 2008 to 2014 the Secure Communities program checked the fingerprints of everyone booked into local jails against immigration databases; a 2014 study found it did not measurably reduce crime.","start":35.82,"end":49.02,"words":[[35.86,36.13],[36.13,36.95],[36.95,37.09],[37.09,37.84],[37.84,37.97],[37.97,38.38],[38.38,39.07],[39.07,39.62],[39.62,39.96],[39.96,40.09],[40.09,40.85],[40.85,40.98],[40.98,41.46],[41.46,41.73],[41.73,42.01],[42.01,42.42],[42.42,42.83],[42.83,43.24],[43.24,43.92],[43.92,44.74],[44.98,45.12],[45.12,45.87],[45.87,46.21],[46.21,46.55],[46.55,46.69],[46.69,46.89],[46.89,47.1],[47.1,47.71],[47.71,48.12],[48.12,48.53]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Racial profiling","start":49.92,"end":51.8,"words":[[49.96,50.59],[50.59,51.65]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In Melendres v. Arpaio (2013), a federal court found that Maricopa County, Arizona, deputies under Sheriff Joe Arpaio had racially profiled Latino drivers during immigration sweeps.","start":52.5,"end":67.17,"words":[[52.54,52.7],[52.7,53.34],[53.34,53.58],[53.98,54.47],[54.47,55.43],[55.71,55.88],[55.88,56.44],[56.44,56.68],[56.68,57.08],[57.08,57.32],[57.32,58.05],[58.05,58.61],[58.89,59.62],[59.9,60.54],[60.54,60.86],[60.86,61.26],[61.26,61.59],[61.59,62.07],[62.07,62.31],[62.31,62.87],[62.87,63.6],[63.6,64.16],[64.16,64.72],[64.72,65.29],[65.29,66.09],[66.09,66.57]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Arpaio was later convicted of contempt for defying the court's orders, and was pardoned in 2017.","start":67.52,"end":74.5,"words":[[67.56,68.01],[68.01,68.24],[68.24,68.62],[68.62,69.29],[69.29,69.44],[69.44,70.05],[70.05,70.2],[70.2,70.72],[70.72,70.88],[70.88,71.18],[71.18,71.55],[71.82,72.04],[72.04,72.27],[72.27,72.72],[72.72,72.87],[72.87,74.0]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In September 2025 the Supreme Court allowed immigration stops in the Los Angeles area to resume while a challenge to their reliance on factors including apparent ethnicity continues (see “Borders”).","start":74.85,"end":87.81,"words":[[74.9,75.05],[75.05,75.67],[75.67,76.9],[76.9,77.05],[77.05,77.51],[77.51,77.75],[77.75,78.13],[78.13,78.9],[78.9,79.28],[79.28,79.44],[79.44,79.59],[79.59,79.82],[79.82,80.44],[80.44,80.82],[80.82,80.98],[80.98,81.44],[81.44,81.75],[81.75,81.9],[81.9,82.51],[82.51,82.67],[82.67,82.9],[82.9,83.51],[83.51,83.67],[83.67,84.13],[84.13,84.75],[84.75,85.28],[85.28,85.9],[85.9,86.59],[86.59,86.74],[86.74,87.21]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Detention","start":88.71,"end":89.58,"words":[[88.77,89.43]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Immigration detention reached record numbers in 2025.","start":90.28,"end":94.62,"words":[[90.32,91.03],[91.03,91.61],[91.61,91.97],[91.97,92.33],[92.33,92.76],[92.76,92.9],[92.9,94.12]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Detention centers are often run by private companies or county jails under contract.","start":94.97,"end":100.51,"words":[[95.01,95.62],[95.62,96.08],[96.08,96.16],[96.16,96.46],[96.46,96.69],[96.69,96.92],[96.92,97.46],[97.46,98.07],[98.07,98.14],[98.14,98.6],[98.6,99.06],[99.06,99.37],[99.37,100.05]]},{"el":"s2","text":"News investigations in 2025 found that U.S. citizens were among the people stopped and detained by immigration agents.","start":100.86,"end":109.15,"words":[[100.91,101.18],[101.18,102.15],[102.15,102.29],[102.29,103.39],[103.39,103.74],[103.74,103.94],[103.94,104.29],[104.63,105.18],[105.18,105.32],[105.32,105.6],[105.6,105.74],[105.74,106.08],[106.08,106.43],[106.43,106.63],[106.63,107.12],[107.12,107.32],[107.32,108.01],[108.01,108.63]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Do sanctuary policies affect crime?","start":110.05,"end":112.83,"words":[[110.09,110.23],[110.23,110.97],[110.97,111.48],[111.48,111.85],[111.85,112.29]]},{"el":"s3","text":"“Sanctuary” policies limit how much local police help with federal immigration enforcement, for example by declining to hold people on ICE detainer requests without a judicial warrant.","start":113.53,"end":125.83,"words":[[113.58,114.34],[114.34,114.87],[114.87,115.25],[115.25,115.47],[115.47,115.77],[115.77,116.23],[116.23,116.61],[116.61,116.91],[116.91,117.13],[117.13,117.66],[117.66,118.42],[118.42,119.18],[119.44,119.59],[119.59,120.2],[120.2,120.42],[120.42,121.1],[121.1,121.25],[121.25,121.63],[121.63,122.01],[122.01,122.16],[122.16,122.39],[122.39,122.92],[122.92,123.52],[123.52,123.97],[123.97,124.12],[124.12,124.73],[124.73,125.26]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Supporters say they keep immigrants willing to report crimes and serve as witnesses; opponents say they release people who should be deported.","start":126.18,"end":134.85,"words":[[126.23,126.77],[126.77,127.01],[127.01,127.24],[127.24,127.48],[127.48,128.18],[128.18,128.57],[128.57,128.73],[128.73,129.12],[129.12,129.59],[129.59,129.82],[129.82,130.05],[130.05,130.21],[130.21,130.91],[131.19,131.89],[131.89,132.12],[132.12,132.36],[132.36,132.75],[132.75,133.14],[133.14,133.29],[133.29,133.53],[133.53,133.68],[133.68,134.31]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Most studies find no increase in crime from sanctuary policies, but the debate continues and federal and state laws on the question keep changing.","start":135.2,"end":144.69,"words":[[135.25,135.61],[135.61,136.04],[136.04,136.4],[136.4,136.62],[136.62,137.05],[137.05,137.19],[137.19,137.55],[137.55,137.84],[137.84,138.56],[138.56,139.14],[139.39,139.61],[139.61,139.75],[139.75,140.18],[140.18,140.83],[140.83,141.05],[141.05,141.55],[141.55,141.76],[141.76,142.12],[142.12,142.34],[142.34,142.48],[142.48,142.63],[142.63,143.2],[143.2,143.42],[143.42,144.14]]},{"el":"h4","text":"What families can do","start":145.59,"end":147.3,"words":[[145.64,145.93],[145.93,146.62],[146.62,146.92],[146.92,147.11]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Know your rights at home and on the street (see “Your rights with police”).","start":148.0,"end":152.58,"words":[[148.05,148.32],[148.32,148.49],[148.49,148.93],[148.93,149.1],[149.1,149.45],[149.45,149.71],[149.71,149.89],[149.89,150.06],[150.06,150.5],[150.5,150.67],[150.67,150.85],[150.85,151.28],[151.28,151.54],[151.54,152.07]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Make a family preparedness plan: who picks up the children, where documents are, and a lawyer's number memorized.","start":152.93,"end":160.53,"words":[[152.98,153.27],[153.27,153.42],[153.42,153.86],[153.86,154.59],[154.59,154.96],[155.22,155.36],[155.36,155.66],[155.66,155.8],[155.8,155.95],[155.95,156.61],[156.87,157.09],[157.09,157.82],[157.82,157.97],[158.22,158.44],[158.44,158.59],[158.59,158.96],[158.96,159.32],[159.32,160.06]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Carry a “red card” stating your rights.","start":160.88,"end":163.5,"words":[[160.93,161.23],[161.23,161.38],[161.38,161.61],[161.61,161.83],[161.83,162.36],[162.36,162.5],[162.5,162.95]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Connect with local rapid-response networks and legal services.","start":163.85,"end":169.34,"words":[[163.9,164.47],[164.47,164.75],[164.75,165.33],[165.33,166.47],[166.47,167.14],[167.14,167.43],[167.43,167.9],[167.9,168.67]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Report false reports to police or immigration authorities that target people because of their ethnicity; that is exactly what CAREN-style laws address.","start":169.69,"end":178.92,"words":[[169.73,170.11],[170.11,170.42],[170.42,170.88],[170.88,171.04],[171.04,171.42],[171.42,171.5],[171.5,172.27],[172.27,172.89],[172.89,173.12],[173.12,173.5],[173.5,173.89],[173.89,174.27],[174.27,174.43],[174.43,174.66],[174.66,175.35],[175.62,175.85],[175.85,176.01],[176.01,176.63],[176.63,176.86],[176.86,177.63],[177.63,177.86],[177.86,178.32]]}]}